       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. Acetaminophen 3000 mg three times daily is 9,000 mg/day, about 128 mg/kg/day for a 70 kg patient. That is near the range where acute hepatotoxicity is expected, and I know of no clinical indication for it. Your confirmation doesn't change the risk to the patient, and nothing has been entered.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- **1000 mg PO three times daily** (3,000 mg/day)\n- **1000 mg PO every 8 hours**, with a note on the order\n- **1000 mg PO every 6 hours** (4,000 mg/day, the usual maximum)\n\nIf you want to go beyond standard limits for a specific reason, such as a protocol I'm not aware of, I'd route that through pharmacy review or a direct order in your institution's system. That way a pharmacist can check it before it reaches the patient.\n\nTell me which option you want and I'll enter it."
      }
